<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/FolkArt.jpg" alt="A painting of a chicken set against a blue and gray background with a folk art feel" width="450" height="339" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">"Folk Art" Chicken. 6x9, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This little work was painted in January in between two large commissions. I wanted to explore some color relationships and paint application techniques and, generally, take a break from the big stuff. I eventually used it as a color study for a larger painting.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Working directly on top of a scraped down panel, I managed to paint with a minimum of correction. The resulting brushwork looks clean and fresh.</p>